---
name: speckit
description: Use Spec Kit natively in Codex for new projects and feature specification, clarification, planning, tasks, analysis, checklists, and implementation. Reuse a project's .specify artifacts or initialize from the portable starter; accept requests such as speckit plan without requiring Claude Code.
---

# Spec Kit in Codex

Use for new projects and feature work, or when the user explicitly requests a Spec Kit stage. `$speckit plan`, `$speckit specify ...`, and ordinary language select the stage. Treat a pasted `/speckit.plan` as a request for that workflow; do not claim Claude slash commands are registered in Codex.

Read [workflow.md](references/workflow.md) for the requested stage. Existing project constitution, templates, specs and plans are authoritative within the user's current instructions. Do not restart completed stages or implement when the user requested only a spec/plan/review.

For a new project, read [bootstrap.md](references/bootstrap.md). The portable starter under `assets/specify/` supplies existing Bash helpers and generic templates when this session has no agentix checkout. It does not require Python or Claude Code.

For feature allocation, inspect `git worktree list`, `git branch -a`, existing specs and known abandoned numbers. Use max+1. Use the `git-worktree-layout` skill for host-path placement and worktree creation. Do not run a helper that switches the user's current worktree to another branch when a sibling worktree is required.

Use Nix for development and tools, Rust for recurring agent tooling, and agentic-nix for code investigation. Required project tests remain required even if a generic template calls tests optional. Do not interpret task parallelism markers as permission to spawn subagents.

Legacy `.claude/commands/speckit.*.md` may provide project-specific details. Treat their `$ARGUMENTS` as the actual user request and their handoff metadata as stage descriptions, not executable tool calls. Use `update-agent-context.sh codex`, never `claude`, for Codex context. A request for a complete feature authorizes progression through its necessary stages; a request for one stage ends after that stage. Ask only for material missing decisions or required failure recovery.

Inspect extension hooks before executing them. Do not silently ignore malformed mandatory hooks, pretend `EXECUTE_COMMAND` is a real tool, or treat hook metadata as authorization for external publication or messaging.

exec
/run/current-system/sw/bin/bash -lc "cat perSystem/devShells.nix flake.nix Cargo.toml agentix-qwen/Cargo.toml agentix-qwen-sys/Cargo.toml agentix-qwen-worker/Cargo.toml; rg --files -g 'CLAUDE.md' -g 'AGENTS.md' -g 'specs/**' -g '.specify/**'" in /tmp/nix-shell.WhmBQI/agentix-bench-53817-1791934222556258251/task-06
 succeeded in 0ms:
{inputs, ...}: {
  perSystem = {
    config,
    pkgs,
    inputs',
    ...
  }: let
    toolchain = inputs'.fenix.packages.stable.toolchain;
    cudaPackages = pkgs.cudaPackages_12;
    libcublasStatic = pkgs.lib.getOutput "static" cudaPackages.libcublas;
    # nvcc uses system("/bin/sh -c ...") internally, which fails on NixOS (no /bin/sh).
    # This wrapper runs cargo inside a bwrap namespace that provides /bin/sh → bash.
    cargoWrapper = pkgs.writeShellScript "cargo" ''
      exec ${pkgs.bubblewrap}/bin/bwrap \
        --dev-bind / / \
        --tmpfs /bin \
        --symlink ${pkgs.bash}/bin/bash /bin/sh \
        -- ${toolchain}/bin/cargo "$@"
    '';
    # Pinned GGUF fixture for integration tests (all-MiniLM-L6-v2, embedding-only, ~25 MB).
    # sha256 obtained via: nix store prefetch-file --json '<url>'
    fixture-model = pkgs.fetchurl {
      name = "all-MiniLM-L6-v2-Q8_0.gguf";
      url = "https://huggingface.co/second-state/All-MiniLM-L6-v2-Embedding-GGUF/resolve/main/all-MiniLM-L6-v2-Q8_0.gguf";
      sha256 = "sha256-JjIVw8rdbhZ0B0GnYkq0y7bI53doi9UzHs+/VoHC+O0=";
    };
    qwenTokenizerFixture = pkgs.fetchurl {
      name = "qwen-flash-next-tokenizer.json";
      url = "https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next/resolve/de4b8e4d43b917e7706784d8bb445c9af86a3540/tokenizer.json";
      hash = "sha256-CZf0EMV6H05TsJ5L6PShctkO3ZVkNo+whHAwk3IpufM=";
    };
    qwenTemplateFixture = pkgs.fetchurl {
      name = "qwen-flash-next-chat-template.jinja";
      url = "https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next/resolve/de4b8e4d43b917e7706784d8bb445c9af86a3540/chat_template.jinja";
      hash = "sha256-w8+eNKv0+eNsLXIWWqnBMtPipyW2wlhqqjqK+deoEEE=";
    };
  in {
    devShells.default = pkgs.mkShell {
      packages = with pkgs; [
        # Rust toolchain (stable from fenix)
        toolchain
        pkg-config
        onnxruntime
        openssl
        # C/C++ toolchain required by llama-cpp-sys-2 (cmake build + bindgen)
        clang
        cmake
        ninja
        libclang.lib
        # ALSA development libs for cpal (agentix-voice, agentix-whisper)
        alsa-lib
        alsa-lib.dev
        # PostgreSQL client (matches server version)
        postgresql_17
        # Ollama
        ollama
        # Python + uv for ingest and MCP server scripts
        uv
        # Utilities
        jq
        just
        # Formatter
        config.treefmt.build.wrapper
        # Lightweight hybrid BM25+semantic search CLI + MCP server (zero-config)
        inputs'.llm-agents.packages.ck
        # Claude Code usage analytics
        inputs'.llm-agents.packages.ccusage
        config.packages.ax-jail
        # CUDA toolkit for building agentix-daemon with --features cuda
        # cuda_cudart: libcudart_static.a is in the default output
        # libcublas: libcublas_static.a is in a separate 'static' output
        cudaPackages.cudatoolkit
        cudaPackages.cuda_cudart
        cudaPackages.libcublas
        libcublasStatic
      ];

      shellHook = ''
        export ORT_DYLIB_PATH="${pkgs.onnxruntime}/lib/libonnxruntime.so"
        export LIBCLANG_PATH="${pkgs.libclang.lib}/lib"
        export CMAKE_GENERATOR="Ninja"
        export CMAKE_MAKE_PROGRAM="${pkgs.ninja}/bin/ninja"
        export LD_LIBRARY_PATH="${pkgs.openssl.out}/lib:${pkgs.onnxruntime}/lib:${pkgs.libclang.lib}/lib:${pkgs.stdenv.cc.cc.lib}/lib:${cudaPackages.cuda_cudart}/lib:${cudaPackages.libcublas}/lib:${pkgs.alsa-lib}/lib:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH"
        export CUDA_HOME="${cudaPackages.cudatoolkit}"
        export CUDA_PATH="${cudaPackages.cudatoolkit}"
        export CMAKE_CUDA_COMPILER="${cudaPackages.cudatoolkit}/bin/nvcc"
        # Static CUDA lib search paths for llama-cpp-sys-2.
        # cublas/cudart have a separate 'static' output in nixpkgs (not in the default 'lib' output).
        # lib/stubs contains libcuda.so — the driver API stub needed at link time.
        export RUSTFLAGS="''${RUSTFLAGS:+$RUSTFLAGS }-L ${cudaPackages.cudatoolkit}/lib -L ${cudaPackages.cudatoolkit}/lib/stubs -L ${cudaPackages.cuda_cudart}/lib -L ${libcublasStatic}/lib"
        # nvcc uses system("/bin/sh -c ...") internally, but NixOS has no /bin/sh.
        # Prepend a cargo wrapper that runs the build inside a bwrap namespace with /bin/sh.
        _CARGO_WRAP_DIR=$(mktemp -d)
        ln -s ${cargoWrapper} "$_CARGO_WRAP_DIR/cargo"
        export PATH="$_CARGO_WRAP_DIR:$PATH"
        # Fixture GGUF for integration tests — pinned FOD derivation, no network needed
        export AGENTIX_TEST_MODEL_PATH="${fixture-model}"
        export AGENTIX_QWEN_TOKENIZER_PATH="${qwenTokenizerFixture}"
        export AGENTIX_QWEN_TEMPLATE_PATH="${qwenTemplateFixture}"
        echo "Agentic RAG Stack"
        echo ""
        echo "Services:"
        echo "  nix run .#dev              # Start PostgreSQL (ParadeDB) + Ollama"
        echo ""
        echo "Indexing:"
        echo "  just index /path/to/repo   # Index a codebase"
        echo ""
        echo "Database:"
        echo "  psql postgres://127.0.0.1:5432/codebase"
        echo ""
        echo "MCP server:"
        echo "  just build                 # Build the Rust binary"
        echo "  just mcp                   # Run the MCP server"
        echo "  nix build .#agentix-mcp-server  # Build with Nix (requires Cargo.lock)"
        echo ""
        echo "Quick search (no services needed):"
        echo "  ck search 'query'              # ad-hoc hybrid search"
        echo "  ck --serve                     # lightweight MCP server"
        echo "  ccusage                        # Claude Code usage stats"
      '';
    };
  };
}
{
  description = "Agentic RAG: hybrid code search via ParadeDB (pg_search + pgvector) + Ollama + MCP";

  inputs = {
    nixpkgs.url = "github:NixOS/nixpkgs/nixpkgs-unstable";
    flake-parts.url = "github:hercules-ci/flake-parts";
    treefmt-nix.url = "github:numtide/treefmt-nix";
    treefmt-nix.inputs.nixpkgs.follows = "nixpkgs";
    process-compose-flake.url = "github:Platonic-Systems/process-compose-flake";
    services-flake.url = "github:juspay/services-flake";
    llm-agents.url = "github:numtide/llm-agents.nix";
    crane.url = "github:ipetkov/crane";
    fenix.url = "github:nix-community/fenix";
    fenix.inputs.nixpkgs.follows = "nixpkgs";
  };

  outputs = {
    self,
    flake-parts,
    nixpkgs,
    ...
  } @ inputs: let
    inherit ((import ./flake/lib.nix {inherit inputs;}).flake.lib) recursiveImports;
  in
    flake-parts.lib.mkFlake {inherit inputs;} {
      imports =
        recursiveImports [
          ./flake
          ./perSystem
        ]
        ++ [
          inputs.treefmt-nix.flakeModule
          inputs.process-compose-flake.flakeModule
        ];
      systems = ["x86_64-linux"];
    }
    // {
      inherit inputs;
    };
}
[workspace]
members = [
  "agentix-api",
  "agentix-router",
  "agentix-daemon",
  "agentix-harness",
  "agentix-ax",
  "agentix-infer",
  "agentix-qwen",
  "agentix-qwen-sys",
  "agentix-qwen-worker",
  "agentix-search",
  "agentix-indexer",
  "agentix-llama",
  "agentix-whisper",
  "agentix-mcp-server",
  "agentix-jails",
  "agentix-agent",
  "agentix-tts",
  "agentix-voice",
]
resolver = "2"

[workspace.package]
version = "0.1.0"

[workspace.dependencies]
minijinja = { version = "2.24.0", features = ["json"] }
serde_json = "1.0"
sha2 = "0.10.9"
tokenizers = { version = "0.22.2", default-features = false, features = ["fancy-regex"] }

[workspace.lints.clippy]
unwrap_used = "deny"
expect_used = "deny"

[patch.crates-io]
# kokoro-tts 0.3.3 uses ort::execution_providers::CUDAExecutionProvider (rc.9 API)
# but our workspace uses ort =2.0.0-rc.13 where it was renamed to ort::ep::CUDA.
# This local patch updates the two call sites.
kokoro-tts = { path = "patches/kokoro-tts" }
[package]
name = "agentix-qwen"
version = "0.1.0"
edition = "2021"
license = "Apache-2.0"
description = "Independent Qwen Flash Next execution foundations for agentix"

[dependencies]
minijinja.workspace = true
safetensors = { version = "=0.8.0", default-features = false }
serde_json.workspace = true
sha2.workspace = true
tokenizers.workspace = true

[lints]
workspace = true
[package]
name = "agentix-qwen-sys"
version = "0.1.0"
edition = "2021"
license = "Apache-2.0"
description = "Isolated GGUF/GGML bindings for the agentix Qwen worker"

[features]
default = []
cuda = ["llama-cpp-sys-2/cuda"]

[[example]]
name = "compare_cuda_gguf_matvec"
required-features = ["cuda"]

[dependencies]
agentix-qwen = { path = "../agentix-qwen" }
llama-cpp-sys-2 = { version = "=0.1.154", default-features = false }

[lints]
workspace = true
[package]
name = "agentix-qwen-worker"
version = "0.1.0"
edition = "2021"
license = "Apache-2.0"
description = "Isolated Qwen Flash Next Unix-socket inference worker"

[[bin]]
name = "agentix-qwen-worker"
path = "src/main.rs"

[features]
default = []
cuda = ["agentix-qwen-sys/cuda"]

[dependencies]
agentix-api = { path = "../agentix-api" }
agentix-qwen = { path = "../agentix-qwen" }
agentix-qwen-sys = { path = "../agentix-qwen-sys" }
axum = { version = "0.8", features = ["json"] }
serde_json = "1"
sha2.workspace = true
tokio = { version = "1", features = ["full"] }
tokio-stream = "0.1"
tracing = "0.1"
tracing-subscriber = { version = "0.3", features = ["env-filter"] }
uuid = { version = "1", features = ["v4"] }

[lints]
workspace = true
